Please, note that by "vague syntax" above I mean that the principle of
least effort applies not only to tenses, number but even to syntactic tree.
Namely, language might omit declaring to which head a branch is attached.

When English parsers force an assumption that a branch must be attached to
a strictly specified head they break this principle.

E.g. when in {mi citka lo plise} you derive tense from context similarly
when using vague clauses you derive the head it is attached to from context.


I just want to separate what I said about vague syntax from what you just
suggested for multibranching.

